            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Here’s what’s **newest around Azure AI as of today (Monday, August 3, 2026)**—split into *official product updates* vs *broader “news” coverage*.\n\n## Official Azure / Azure AI updates (most reliable)\n- **Public Preview: “AI Gateway” tier in Azure API Management (July 2026)** — a dedicated API Management experience optimized for AI workloads, aimed at governing and securing exposure of AI assets like models, MCP servers, and tools. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- **Azure Blog: “GPT‑5.6 now available in Microsoft Foundry” (July 9, 2026)** — Microsoft is positioning Foundry as the primary “Azure AI” surface for frontier models + agent capabilities. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n- **Azure Blog: “Claude in Microsoft Foundry is now generally available” (June 29, 2026)** — Claude hosted on Azure and described as geared toward moving agent experiments into production. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n\n## Today’s broader “Azure AI” news (partner + industry)\n- **Microsoft earnings coverage is emphasizing Azure’s AI-driven growth** (multiple outlets summarizing recent results and AI demand). ([crn.com](https://www.crn.com/news/cloud/2026/aws-vs-microsoft-vs-google-cloud-earnings-q2-2026-face-off))  \n- **Ongoing infrastructure push for AI inference**: multiple reports say Microsoft is rolling out / adopting **AMD’s “Helios”** platform for Azure AI inference-related expansion. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/technology/microsoft-to-roll-out-amd-helios-for-ai-inference-on-azure/ar-AA28odHr))  \n\n## If you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (Foundry vs Azure AI Studio/Services vs infra), I can narrow this to the *single most relevant* set of updates for your use case.",
